```java
public class Account {
    private static int accountCount = 0;
    private String owner;
    private double balance;

    public Account(String owner, double initialDeposit) {
        this.owner = owner;
        if (initialDeposit > 0) {
            balance = initialDeposit;
        } else {
            balance = 0;
        }
        accountCount++;
    }

    public String getOwner() { return owner; }

    public double getBalance() { return balance; }

    public void deposit(double amount) {
        if (amount > 0) {
            balance += amount;
        }
    }

    public boolean withdraw(double amount) {
        if (amount <= 0 || amount > balance) {
            return false;
        }
        balance -= amount;
        return true;
    }

    public static int getAccountCount() { return accountCount; }
}
```
The counter is `static` so that it is shared by every `Account`; the constructor increments it once for each object created.

